  "answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative led by Marcus Cole, launching in Q3 2023 with a kickoff on July 15th. The project aims to enhance security and accessibility using AI. Key milestones include a call for AI-driven data visualization ideas (due July 20th), initial findings showing a potential 20% efficiency increase (discussed August 5th), and team expansions adding members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing. The project has progressed through design and testing phases, with a development phase led by Omar Jensen starting next month. A training budget of $15,000 was approved for coding and management teams. The team celebrated the completion of the testing phase on October 10th, and feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November."
